- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** The whole-project undo and redo go, because their only state is the aggregate (001 §R '`.ocproj`'; the S4.4 brief names `History.fs`; .spec-md §8: this spec adds no undo history). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/History.fs` (`History.fs:History`: `EditHistory` with `ofPresent`, `push`, `undo` and `redo`) is deleted with its `<Compile>` line (`OpticalConstructor.Storage.fsproj:36`); the comment above `RecentFiles.fs`'s `<Compile>` loses its undo/redo words and gains none. Nothing else in the product names the module. (2) Tests: in `OpticalConstructor.Tests/HistoryTests.fs`, `AC-I7 undo restores the pre-edit project and redo restores the edit` and `AC-I7 undo on empty history returns the input unchanged` (`HistoryTests.fs:48-66`) are deleted with `open OpticalConstructor.Storage.History`. The fixtures `projectWith`, `preEdit` and `edited` stay, because `AC-I6 writeAutosave leaves the .ocproj untouched and writes a distinct .autosave` uses them until step 159. The module doc (`:19-22`) keeps only its autosave sentence and gains none. Afterwards `git grep -n -E "EditHistory|Storage.History" -- Berreman/` finds nothing.

**Acceptance.** After the edit history is deleted, `git grep -n -E "EditHistory|Storage.History" -- Berreman/` MUST find nothing; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, `R-1 bump dedups case-insensitively, pushes most-recent first, and truncates to maxRecent` and `AC-I6 writeAutosave leaves the .ocproj untouched and writes a distinct .autosave` unchanged, the count falling by 2; and build, elevation and the twelve s18 invariants MUST pass.
